prompt:
Create a 1536x1024 true-transparent RGBA sprite sheet for JAMVERSE '96: EXACTLY eight unique, complete full-body poses in a strict four-column by two-row grid, row-major. One whole Dorian Mycel per cell. Match the attached identity/gameplay reference: compact adult human basketball player, warm medium-brown skin, clean-shaven strong-browed face, short dense vivid-purple curls, purple Chicago Condas kit with silver/lavender edging, dark knee pads, purple wristbands, purple/silver basketball shoes. Preserve his identity, face, curls, skin and proportions throughout.

Right-facing right-handed layup, advancing toward image-right. The ball is separate game art: never draw a ball, sphere, seams or prop. No court, basket, floor, shadow, background, glow, text, numbers, logo, border, grid line or extra person. True transparent gutters and exterior; bold-outlined 1990s arcade pixel art. Complete two-arm, two-hand, two-leg, two-shoe anatomy; no clipping.

0 controlled approach stride, hands mime ball at waist;
1 gathers into both hands and plants for takeoff;
2 launches off one foot, right knee rises, ball-miming hands lift;
3 airborne, torso leans toward basket, right hand carries invisible ball high;
4 RELEASE at tick10: right arm extends fully toward rim, palm opens after layup;
5 follows through at apex, opposite arm balances;
6 descends, legs prepare to land, empty hands lower;
7 controlled soft landing and balanced recovery.
Exactly eight different connected poses, no repetition; show the entire figure each time. Return only the sprite sheet.
